WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:04.501
-Our next guest has his comedy
special, "37 &amp; Single,"

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:06.467
streaming now on Netflix.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.901
Please welcome
the very funny Jared Freid!

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.767
-I was just hanging out
with my parents.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:22.467
Anyone hang out
with their parents still?

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.467
The only problem is
you don't know

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:31.234
if it's going to be a fun hang
or a judgmental hang, right?

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:33.167
My mom will be like,
"Let's have a drink.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:36.534
Have a drink!
Come on, have a drink!"

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:39.200
And then, the next morning,
I walk into the kitchen.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.100
She's at the table.
It's dimly lit.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:46.868
She's like, "We have to talk
about the drinking."

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:49.901
You ever been to an intervention
with your own dealer?

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.701
Your parents aren't going
to change, though.

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:59.834
Never. My mom is never going
to pronounce Chipotle correctly.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.200
She could be on a game show.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.634
The host would be like,
"For $2 million,

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.934
just say Chipotle."

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.734
She'd immediately
make herself the victim.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:11.801
She'd be like,
"Everyone is yelling at me."

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.467
The host would be like,
"No one is yelling at you.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:17.133
For $2 million,
just say Chipotle."

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.934
She'd be like,
"This is ridiculous."

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.701
Chip-o-tal."

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.133
I'm judgy of people's orders,

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.501
but people are judgy
of my orders, too.

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:30.501
You know, I went on
a bachelor party in 2016,

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:34.501
and I ordered
a skinny margarita.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:36.901
That's been my nickname
for seven years.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.267
Every time I hang out
with my friends,

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:43.701
some old lady is like, "Why do
they call you Bethenny Frankel?"

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.100
I judge my mom's orders.
She goes to Starbucks.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.434
You ever go to Starbucks
with your mom?

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.534
It's a show.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:55.200
My mom walks in like
she's the lead of a '90s sitcom.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.200
She's like, "Hi, everybody!"

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.267
And then she goes up
to a teenage barista

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:03.334
and just screams
coffee ingredients.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.534
They make no sense.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.100
She went up --
Last time we went, she goes,

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:14.601
I'll have an iced mocha,
two-scoop, dolce, frothy top.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.667
You know.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:21.968
She said, "You know."
That was the craziest part.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.767
The teenage barista
never looked up.

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:30.300
She just goes, "I got it.
She's here every day."

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.767
Here's the actual order.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:35.267
Iced mocha latte with two pumps
of cinnamon-dolce sweetener,

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:37.934
steamed skim milk on top.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:41.634
"Scoops" are apparently pumps.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:46.000
That teenage barista is the
greatest detective of our time.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.567
Right? I just imagine
her in her bedroom.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.367
There's, like,
boy-band posters everywhere,

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:53.267
a picture of my mom,
red string out to all the clues.

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:54.367
She's sitting there
with a cigarette.

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:57.868
She's like, "Dolce.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.067
Frothy top."

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.567
I want to go on
every errand with my mom.

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:02.634
Not the places that know her,

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.000
not the places that
don't know her,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.534
the ones in the middle,
the ones getting to know her.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.133
Right? The place where she walks
in and she's like,

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.434
"Hi, everybody,"
and five high-school kids

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:13.167
are like, "Oh, no!"

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.367
Right? She goes to the market.
She goes to the deli counter.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:18.033
She's like,
"Shrimp-chicken thingy."

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:20.200
You see the deli guy.
"Okay, shrimp woman's back.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.033
Here we go.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:26.133
Remember, shrimp means
salami, 1/4 pound.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:28.100
She wants it sliced thin,
but not too thin,

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.334
but kind of thin.

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.434
Chicken thingy --
not a chicken, not a turkey.

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:36.767
We'll go provolone.
We got nothing to lose."

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:40.300
She's just not a communicator,
even over texts.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.434
She texts "LOL" to everything.

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:48.133
"LOL. LOL." I hate LOL.
It's a dishonest acronym.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:49.934
Everyone texts "LOL,"
but you've never seen someone

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.234
with their phone in their hand
just in the middle

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:55.067
of the street, just like...
[ Laughs ]

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.801
It's dishonest.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:00.267
I only send honest texting
acronyms, only honest ones,

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:05.767
like "TITTTITWAWSD."

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:09.000
"This is the third time
I've texted, what's up,

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.801
are we still dating?"

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:16.434
"YTACIGAYP."

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:21.200
"Your texts are coming in green,
are you poor?"

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:31.167
"PRMFTGTILTOTCIAKGETTTAFSE."

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.767
"Please remove me
from this group text,

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:35.300
I've lost track
of the conversation

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.701
and I keep getting excited
thinking the text

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:37.734
is from someone else."

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.267
Thank you, guys.
I'm Jared Freid.

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:42.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.634
Two scoops. Two scoops.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:47.334
-Yeah.
-The best. Jared Freid!

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:48.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:52.801
"37 &amp; Single"
is available now on Netflix.

